{
  "reviews": {
    "r1": {
      "O": {
        "1": {
          "evidence": "Chart title: 'Additional Promotion Weeks: Ad Spend vs Sales'. Plot shows five labeled weekly points (Week 7 to Week 11).",
          "status": "supported"
        },
        "2": {
          "evidence": "Chart area contains no visible legend, control group, profitability measure, cost threshold, causal annotation, or full-data analysis.",
          "status": "supported"
        }
      },
      "B": {
        "reading_checked": "If approving broader spend requires evidence that spend itself, rather than other promotion-week factors, drove sales or that the increase is financially justified, then a five-point observational scatterplot without controls, costs, margins, or causal analysis is insufficient and the appropriate action is to request full-data analysis.",
        "evidence": "The condition 'Applies when approval requires causal, profitability, or broader-data validation; none of those requirements or results is visibly supplied.' is met. The chart provides no evidence of causality, profitability, or broader data. The chart is an observational scatterplot with no controls or financial metrics.",
        "status": "supported"
      }
    },
    "r2": {
      "O": {
        "1": {
          "evidence": "Horizontal axis label: 'Advertising Spend ($ thousands)'. Vertical axis label: 'Sales ($ thousands)'.",
          "status": "supported"
        },
        "2": {
          "evidence": "Points are labeled Week 7, Week 8, Week 9, Week 10, Week 11. They progress from lower-left to upper-right on the page.",
          "status": "supported"
        },
        "3": {
          "evidence": "Week 7: x≈30, y≈65. Week 11: x≈70, y≈160.",
          "status": "supported"
        }
      },
      "B": {
        "reading_checked": "If the horizontal axis encodes advertising spend and the vertical axis encodes sales, both in $ thousands, then points farther right and higher represent weeks with greater plotted spend and greater plotted sales; if this five-week pattern is accepted as sufficient evidence for budget expansion despite no causal-validation requirement, approve broader ad spend increase.",
        "evidence": "The condition 'Applies only if the axis labels correctly bind to the plotted points and an observed positive association is considered sufficient for approval.' is met. The axis labels correctly bind to the plotted points. The pattern shows a clear positive association: as spend increases, sales increase. The reading implies that if this pattern is considered sufficient, then approve the increase. The chart provides no information about causal validation requirements, so the condition for approval is met.",
        "status": "supported"
      }
    }
  }
}
